* {{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/br/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|title=Future Nostalgia de Dua Lipa|publisher=Apple Music (BR)|language=pt|access-date=9 August 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200809165634/https://music.apple.com/br/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|archive-date=9 August 2020}}
* {{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/gb/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|title=Future Nostalgia by Dua Lipa|publisher=Apple Music (GB)|access-date=9 August 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200801031111/https://music.apple.com/gb/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|archive-date=1 August 2020}}
* {{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/jp/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|title=Dua Lipaの「Future Nostalgia」|publisher=Apple Music (JP)|language=ja|access-date=9 August 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200809165651/https://music.apple.com/jp/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|archive-date=9 August 2020}}
* {{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/us/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|title=Future Nostalgia by Dua Lipa|publisher=Apple Music (US)|access-date=9 August 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623154254/https://music.apple.com/us/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|archive-date=23 June 2020}}
* {{cite web|url=https://music.apple.com/za/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|title=Future Nostalgia by Dua Lipa|publisher=Apple Music (ZA)|access-date=9 August 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200809165701/https://music.apple.com/za/album/future-nostalgia/1495799403|archive-date=9 August 2020}}</ref>

Lipa began by recording the lead vocals, and later some backing vocals and vocals with all the collaborators. They would create different personas with different vocals every time they recorded them. Lipa recalled that she and her co-writers were dancing all through making the song, even if they were experiencing [[writer's block]] or working on the production. After finishing the song, Lipa enlisted the help of [[Stuart Price]] for some additional production. He brought more "bounce" to the song and helped with the [[Bass guitar|bass]] [[Groove (music)|groove]]. He also incorporated a high [[Drone (music)|drone]] synth as a [[disco]] [[Trope (music)|trope]], and a string part in the [[pre-chorus]]. Koz later also enlisted the help of Bosko "Electrospit" Kante to play a [[talk box]].<ref name="Song Exploder" /> "Levitating" helped dictate what the rest of ''Future Nostalgia'' would sound like and where Lipa thought everything made sense, where she had both the "future" and "nostalgia" elements. She called it the "starting point" of the album.<ref name="People" /><ref name="NYTimes" /><ref name="Livestream" />

"Levitating" is an [[electro-disco]], [[nu-disco]], [[pop-funk]] and [[space rock]] song,<!-- Please see talk page for the full details of these genres --><ref name="Allmusic">{{cite web|url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/future-nostalgia-mw0003359848|title=Future Nostalgia - Dua Lipa|publisher=[[AllMusic]]|last=Yeung|first=Neil Z.|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623171025/https://www.allmusic.com/album/future-nostalgia-mw0003359848|archive-date=23 June 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/features/articles/best-albums-2020-ranked|title=The Best Albums of 2020 Ranked|website=[[The Line of Best Fit]]|date=3 December 2020|access-date=5 December 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201205143432/https://www.thelineofbestfit.com/features/articles/best-albums-2020-ranked|archive-date=5 December 2020}}</ref><ref name="Slant Remix">{{cite web|url=https://www.slantmagazine.com/news/listen-dua-lipa-elevates-levitating-with-help-from-madonna-and-missy-elliott/|title=Listen: Dua Lipa Elevates 'Levitating' with Help from Madonna and Missy Elliott|work=[[Slant Magazine]]|last=Camp|first=Alexa|date=13 August 2020|access-date=8 September 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200821143431/https://www.slantmagazine.com/news/listen-dua-lipa-elevates-levitating-with-help-from-madonna-and-missy-elliott/|archive-date=21 August 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|first= Sean |last= Maunier |title= Music Review: Dua Lipa's 'Future Nostalgia'|website= [[Metro Weekly]] |date= 2 April 2020|url= https://www.metroweekly.com/2020/04/music-review-dua-lipas-future-nostalgia/|accessdate= 30 January 2022}}</ref> with [[dance-pop]] and [[power pop]] elements.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.teenvogue.com/story/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-review|title=Dua Lipa 'Future Nostalgia' Review: Dancing As the World Stills|work=[[Teen Vogue]]|last=Cardenas|first=Cat|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200624002842/https://www.teenvogue.com/story/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-review|archive-date=24 June 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.metroweekly.com/2020/04/music-review-dua-lipas-future-nostalgia/|title=Music Review: Dua Lipa's 'Future Nostalgia'|work=[[Metro Weekly]]|last=Maunier|first=Sean|date=2 April 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200731125218/https://www.metroweekly.com/2020/04/music-review-dua-lipas-future-nostalgia/|archive-date=31 July 2020}}</ref><ref name="hotpress">{{cite web|url=https://www.hotpress.com/music/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-22810209|title=Album Review: Dua Lipa, Future Nostalgia|work=[[Hot Press]]|last=O'Toole|first=Lucy|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200731125205/https://www.hotpress.com/music/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-22810209|archive-date=31 July 2020}}</ref> The song incorporates music styles from the [[1970s in music|1970s]], [[1980s in music|1980s]], and [[1990s in music|1990s]] [[Pop music|pop]] and [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/dua-lipas-club-ready-remix-of-levitating-with-madonna-and-missy-elliott-is-here/|title=Dua Lipa's club-ready remix of Levitating with Madonna and Missy Elliott is here|website=[[Gay Times]]|last=Damshenas|first=Sam|date=13 August 2020|access-date=6 November 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201105234220/https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/dua-lipas-club-ready-remix-of-levitating-with-madonna-and-missy-elliott-is-here/|archive-date=5 November 2020}}</ref><ref name="God">{{cite web|url=http://www.godisinthetvzine.co.uk/2020/04/01/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-warner/|title=Dua Lipa - Future Nostalgia (Warner)|work=[[God Is in the TV]]|last=Wright|first=Jonathan|date=1 April 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623195446/http://www.godisinthetvzine.co.uk/2020/04/01/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-warner/|archive-date=23 June 2020}}</ref><ref name="Melodic">{{cite web|url=https://www.melodicmag.com/2020/03/31/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia/|title=Album Review: Dua Lipa // Future Nostalgia|work=[[Melodic (magazine)|Melodic]]|last=Sloman|first=Christine|date=31 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200725173849/https://www.melodicmag.com/2020/03/31/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia/|archive-date=25 July 2020}}</ref> Constructed in [[verse–chorus form]], the song runs for 3 minutes and 23 seconds and is composed in [[Time signature|{{music|time|4|4}} time]] and the [[Key (music)|key]] of [[B minor]], with a [[tempo]] of 103 beats per minute and a [[chord progression]] of Bm<sup>7</sup>—F{{music|sharp}}m<sup>7</sup>—Em<sup>7</sup>.<ref name="Apple Music" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.umusicpub.com/us/Digital-Music-Library/song/433411/dua-lipa-levitating|title=Song Details|publisher=[[Universal Music Publishing Group]]|access-date=19 October 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20201019000014/https://www.umusicpub.com/us/Digital-Music-Library/song/433411/dua-lipa-levitating|archive-date=19 October 2020}}</ref><ref name="MN">{{cite web|url=https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0219642|title=Dua Lipa feat. DaBaby 'Levitating' sheet music in B Minor|date=15 October 2020|publisher=Musicnotes|access-date=19 October 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201018235411/https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0219642|archive-date=18 October 2020}}</ref> It is built around a wonky synth hook, with 1990s choruses and several [[Camp (style)|campy]] disco tropes.<ref name="God" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-review-dance-album-is-sublime/|title=Dua Lipa 'Future Nostalgia' Review: Dance Album Is 'Sublime'|work=[[Us Weekly]]|last=Hautman|first=Nicholas|date=26 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623193247/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-review-dance-album-is-sublime/|archive-date=23 June 2020}}</ref><ref name="Gay Times">{{cite web|url=https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/we-ranked-every-track-on-dua-lipas-excellent-new-album-future-nostalgia/|title=We ranked every track on Dua Lipa's excellent new album Future Nostalgia|work=Gay Times|last=Megarry|first=Daniel|date=26 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200726010309/https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/we-ranked-every-track-on-dua-lipas-excellent-new-album-future-nostalgia/|archive-date=26 July 2020}}</ref> The rest of the production consists of funky synth disco beats,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://riotmag.co/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia|title=Album Review: Dua Lipa // Future Nostalgia|work=Riot Magazine|last=Edwards|first=Caroline|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623165258/https://riotmag.co/album-review-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia|archive-date=23 June 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2020/dec/17/the-50-best-albums-of-2020-no-2-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia|title=The 50 best albums of 2020, No 2: Dua Lipa – Future Nostalgia|website=[[The Guardian]]|last=Solomon|first=Kate|date=17 December 2020|access-date=4 January 2021|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201217130613/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2020/dec/17/the-50-best-albums-of-2020-no-2-dua-lipa-future-nostalgia|archive-date=17 December 2020}}</ref> a "squelchy" bass,<ref name="God" /> "rubbery" basslines, syncopated handclaps,<ref name="NME">{{cite web|url=https://www.nme.com/reviews/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review-2633945|title=Dua Lipa – 'Future Nostalgia' review|work=[[NME]]|last=Daly|first=Rhian|date=24 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200624003110/https://www.nme.com/reviews/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review-2633945|archive-date=24 June 2020}}</ref> nu-disco rhythms,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://jenesaispop.com/2020/07/27/395426/dua-lipa-anuncia-remix-de-levitating-con-madonna-y-missy-elliott-producido-por-the-blessed-madonna/|title=Dua Lipa anuncia remix de 'Levitating' con Madonna y Missy Elliott|work=Jenesaispop|language=es|last=Bardají|first=Jordi|date=27 July 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200731143525/https://jenesaispop.com/2020/07/27/395426/dua-lipa-anuncia-remix-de-levitating-con-madonna-y-missy-elliott-producido-por-the-blessed-madonna/|archive-date=31 July 2020}}</ref> "wonky" and "bizarre" [[synthesizer|synths]],<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/reviews/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review-tracklist-dont-start-now-physical-a9428896.html|title=Dua Lipa – Future Nostalgia review: Pure sonic spandex|work=[[The Independent]]|last=Brown|first=Helen|date=26 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200725170709/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/reviews/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review-tracklist-dont-start-now-physical-a9428896.html|archive-date=25 July 2020}}</ref><ref name="Billboard">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-songs-ranking-9345029/|title=Ranking All 11 Songs on Dua Lipa's 'Future Nostalgia': Critic's Take|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Gracie|first=Bianca|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200623164657/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/9345029/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-songs-ranking|archive-date=23 June 2020}}</ref> an [[Electronic dance music|EDM]] groove,<ref name="LA Times" /> funky guitars, talk box vocals,<ref name="Vulture">{{cite web|url=https://www.vulture.com/2020/03/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review.html|title=Dua Lipa 'Future Nostalgia' Album Review|work=[[New York (magazine)|Vulture]]|last=Jenkins|first=Craig|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200725024050/https://www.vulture.com/2020/03/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-album-review.html|archive-date=25 July 2020}}</ref> a "hypnotic" synth line and disco strings.<ref name="popmatters">{{cite web|url=https://www.popmatters.com/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-2645576792.html?rebelltitem=1#rebelltitem1|title=Dua Lipa: Future Nostalgia|work=[[PopMatters]]|last=Malone|first=Nick|date=27 March 2020|access-date=31 July 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://archive.today/20200726002636/https://www.popmatters.com/dua-lipa-future-nostalgia-2645576792.html|archive-date=26 July 2020}}</ref> The bass, guitars, and talk box give off a disco-funk feeling. Following the first chorus, the instruments are stripped back.<ref name="Slant Rank">{{cite web |date=8 December 2020 |title=The 50 Best Songs of 2020 |url=https://www.slantmagazine.com/features/the-50-best-songs-of-2020/5/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201208222359/https://www.slantmagazine.com/features/the-50-best-songs-of-2020/5/ |archive-date=8 December 2020 |access-date=8 December 2020 |website=[[Slant Magazine]]}}</ref> On his remix, DaBaby adds a new [[pop rap]] verse and intro, over the original's production,<ref name="iHeart DaBaby" /><ref name="Billboard DaBaby" /><ref name="Idolator DaBaby" /> with him serving as an additional writer on the track.<ref name="Dababy credits">{{cite web|url=https://listen.tidal.com/album/156009542/credits|title=Credits / Levitating (feat. DaBaby) / Dua Lipa|date=3 August 2020 |publisher=Tidal|access-date=1 October 2020|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201001222449/https://listen.tidal.com/album/156009542/credits|archive-date=1 October 2020}}</ref>

